      "Diagnostic mismatch: The patient has a 5-month history of waxing/waning pain radiating down the lower extremity in an L4-S1 distribution intensified by lying supine. GTPS is localized peritrochanteric pain aggravated by direct lateral compression or weight-bearing; it does not cause dermatomal lower extremity radicular pain. Superior gluteal nerve pathology is purely motor (Trendelenburg lurch), not sensory radiculopathy.",
